            "review_title": "Review at Tanh Tach - Seafood Society",
            "review_text": "Andy\nTaipei, Taiwan388 contributions\n0\nPlain Basics\nOct 2025 • Solo\nOnline photos of the crab cake drew me to the chef menu at Tanh Tách. Seafood and wagyu dishes showed precise fire control. The hot smoked eel and cold truffle ice cream combo worked surprisingly well. However, excessive local herbs overwhelmed the bulot salad. The simpler courses felt downgraded. The bread was plain white toast instead of the butter-seared version from before. The black chicken soup lacked chicken fat, leaving the broth less infused than before. The entire dinner finished within an hour.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten June 28, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
