            "review_title": "Review at Tanh Tach - Seafood Society",
            "review_text": "Jonathan H\nSingapore68 contributions\n1\nFresh seafood at a beautiful restaurant\nDec 2019\nMy wife, son and I had a great leisurely lunch at Tan Tach Seafood Society restaurant. We chose the 3-course set lunch. For the starter, my wife and I had a beetroot, watermelon salad with ginger sauce. The dish was served with a dramatic flourish as the fog of dry ice gradually disappeared to reveal a light, refreshing salad. My son had the green salad with a vinaigrette dressing and smoked salmon. The salad also had avocado, eggs, tomatoes. The ingredients for both salads were very fresh. For the main all three of us had salmon with pea puree and lime sauce. The salmon was perfectly cooked so that the texture and moist freshness of the fish was retained. Not every restaurant gets salmon right. This restaurant does. The pea puree complemented it well. For dessert, my wife and I had the rice pudding with passion mint sauce. The passion mint sauce in the center of the pudding with sprinkled mint leaves around it gave the dish a really appealing look. My son had the crème brulee with strawberry and rosemary. It was served with a refreshing sorbet. All the dishes not only tasted great they were a visual treat as they were artfully plated. We ended the meal with a perfectly brewed coffee served with a biscuit. The restaurant is stylish with a Vietnamese-European café décor. To get to the restaurant on the 2nd floor you walk past a stunning wall size painting. The service was warm, friendly and prompt. We easily spent an hour and half there enjoying the meal and the ambience. It’s the sort of restaurant where you enjoy your meal at a relaxing pace. The environment is pleasant so you want to stay a bit longer. The next time my family and I go we would like to try some of the seafood that was displayed on ice. You see it upon entering the restaurant on the second floor. It looked delicious!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 30, 2019",
